WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.980
Speaker 1: Okay, let's now get into 2024.

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:08.120
Joe Biden's approval has absolutely collapsed.

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:16.139
Now, I was right there telling you when his
approval was low, but still historically higher

00:00:16.139 --> 00:00:18.270
than many presidents at this point in time.

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:19.270
I was telling you that.

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:25.590
I was saying, yeah, it's low ish, but he's
still doing better than A, B, C, D presidents

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:31.670
at this point in their first term, you have
to go back to the 1940s now to find a first

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:38.239
term president with a lower approval rating
at this point, right July of the second year

00:00:38.239 --> 00:00:40.809
of his presidency than Joe Biden.

00:00:40.809 --> 00:00:42.460
And we're going to get to those numbers.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:48.220
But this is coming at a time where also most
Democrats are saying they don't want Joe Biden

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:49.550
to run in 2024.

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:54.760
Now, I don't believe he is going to run in
2024, but we're going to get to that in a

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:55.760
moment.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:00.510
Most Democrats don't want Biden in 24, a new
poll shows.

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:04.910
President Biden is facing an alarming level
of doubt from inside his own party.

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:11.610
64% of Democratic voters say they would prefer
a new standard bearer in 2024.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:14.690
This is from a New York Times Siena College
poll.

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:19.110
Voters nationwide have soured on his leadership,
giving a meager 33% job approval rating.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:21.270
We'll look at an average of approval rating
in a moment.

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:24.560
It's a little bit higher than that in this
particular poll.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.330
It's at 33%.

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:30.880
Widespread concerns about the economy and
inflation have helped turn the national mood

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:35.100
decidedly dark, both on Biden and the trajectory
of the nation.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:38.710
More than three quarters of registered voters
see the U.S. moving in the wrong direction.

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:43.110
A pervasive sense of pessimism that spans
every corner of the country, every age range,

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:47.250
every racial group, cities, suburbs and rural
areas, and both political parties.

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:51.970
Only 13% of American voters say the nation
is on the right track.

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:54.890
Now, in terms of approval.

00:01:54.890 --> 00:02:00.700
Joe Biden's approval on average is down to
38.6%.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:05.790
This is, as you can see here, the lowest of
his presidency.

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:10.659
He kicked off his presidency in the mid-fifties
and remained there for several months, then

00:02:10.659 --> 00:02:14.989
started seeing a decline last summer as the
COVID surge happened.

00:02:14.989 --> 00:02:18.280
Negative press about getting out of Afghanistan,
etc..

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:22.709
A brief bump towards the end of the year and
then a continued decline.

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:24.629
This is really not good.

00:02:24.629 --> 00:02:29.139
And when you look at historical numbers, which
FiveThirtyEight allows you to do, you now

00:02:29.139 --> 00:02:34.159
see that Joe Biden's approval rating has dipped
below where Donald Trump's was.

00:02:34.159 --> 00:02:35.189
At this point in time.

00:02:35.189 --> 00:02:38.379
We're roughly at day 550.

00:02:38.379 --> 00:02:39.379
Where are we?

00:02:39.379 --> 00:02:40.379
Roughly five.

00:02:40.379 --> 00:02:45.560
But 545 of the presidency, Donald Trump had
a higher approval rating at this point.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:48.420
Barack Obama had a higher approval rating
at this point.

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:51.170
George W Bush had a higher approval rating.

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:52.340
So did Clinton.

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:53.390
George H.W.

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:56.920
Bush was doing far better than then Biden
is now.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:58.360
Reagan was doing better.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:01.419
Jimmy Carter was doing better, although not
by much.

00:03:01.419 --> 00:03:02.950
Gerald Ford was doing better.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:04.390
Nixon was doing better.

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:06.139
LBJ was doing better.

00:03:06.139 --> 00:03:07.389
JFK and Eisenhower.

00:03:07.389 --> 00:03:16.279
You have to go all the way back to Harry Truman
in 1946 to find a president that around day

00:03:16.279 --> 00:03:21.310
545 was had a lower approval than Joe Biden.

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:23.379
That's really, really bad.

00:03:23.379 --> 00:03:29.730
I believe it is time for Joe Biden to soon
say I will not be running for reelection in

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:31.120
2024.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:32.249
Make it public.

00:03:32.249 --> 00:03:33.340
Make it clear.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:38.800
Allow for anyone on the Democratic side to
have time to consider whether they want to

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:44.409
run for president in 2024, decide whether
they want to mount a campaign and to have

00:03:44.409 --> 00:03:47.450
a clean, open primary for 2024.

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:48.799
And I say this for a few reasons.

00:03:48.799 --> 00:03:52.799
Number one, I just don't think Joe Biden wants
to run for reelection.

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:54.029
That's the most important thing.

00:03:54.029 --> 00:03:56.209
It's not about pushing Biden out.

00:03:56.209 --> 00:03:59.090
It's I don't see any indication that he wants
to run.

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:01.680
He'll be 82 at the time.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:05.059
The language continues to be that he intends
to run.

00:04:05.059 --> 00:04:10.400
After Kamala Harris definitively said he was
running the next day, she had to walk it back

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:15.200
because it's very apparent to all of us that
it's not clear that he actually plans to run.

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:18.380
That's the primary reason he doesn't seem
to want to run.

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:20.949
And it's becoming.

00:04:20.949 --> 00:04:25.220
Politically disadvantageous to Democrats,
for everybody to kind of have to pretend like

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:26.220
he is going to run.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:27.530
I just don't think he's running.

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:30.050
Secondly, his approval rating is collapsing.

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:34.840
And whether it's Donald Trump or Ron DeSantis
or whoever on the Republican side, there is

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:40.340
going to be a major uphill battle for the
2024 election.

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:46.860
And it would seem prudent and better to not
rush anyone else into having to decide, Am

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:48.480
I getting in or am I getting out?

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:51.060
Make it clear I'm not going to be running
for reelection now.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:54.810
I'm not actually saying that Biden should
announce this before the midterms.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:58.980
It probably makes sense to wait for the midterms,
but it should be done relatively soon.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:03.810
Again, Biden least popular president at this
point in his first term, dating back to Harry

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:05.950
Truman in the 1940s.

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:09.460
Third, even most Democrats don't want Joe
Biden to run.

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:11.540
So looking at the pulse of the party also
matters.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:17.160
Now, I am right there with you in saying that
even most of those Democrats who would rather

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:22.720
someone other than Biden would almost certainly
vote for Biden if Biden is the nominee.

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:28.890
But it's not particularly reassuring when
it comes to the possibility that the right

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:31.540
will be really motivated in 2024.

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:32.540
Okay.

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:33.540
Sure.

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:37.470
Most Democrats, even if they would rather
someone else, would still vote for Biden.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:41.360
But even if it depresses turnout by a couple
of points, I don't know that it's the the

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:43.250
advantage of the Democratic Party.

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:47.040
Now, there are many good options on the Democratic
side, but the question becomes this Kamala

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:53.790
Harris run and if so, do Biden and the DNC
attempt to sort of anoint her the de facto

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:55.020
nominee?

00:05:55.020 --> 00:06:00.110
She's not popular either, and she may lose
a contested primary, but whatever is going

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:04.890
to happen, there should be time so that Democrats
don't get caught flat footed.

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:09.210
Now, let me say one other thing, because I
already know some of the messages that I'm

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:10.340
going to get.

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:15.960
There's a lot of kind of finger wagging going
on at people who aren't feeling inspired or

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:18.490
confident in Biden 2024.

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:21.540
The finger wagging should probably stop.

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:25.920
I'm not saying I wouldn't vote for Biden over
Trump or DeSantis in 2024.

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:27.160
I would.

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:29.710
I'm not even saying Joe Biden hasn't done
some good things.

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:33.320
He's done many good things, and I've enumerated
them many times.

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:41.280
I'm saying it would be better if Biden said
what most Democrats are thinking and said,

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:43.460
I'm not running for reelection.

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:47.100
We did a great thing here by taking the country
back from Trump.

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:54.600
We did A, B, C, D, and I am clearing the way
for a spirited primary where we are going

00:06:54.600 --> 00:07:01.960
to get, I am sure, a great nominee to go up
against what is going to be a brutally desperate

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:06.060
attempt by Republicans to take back the White
House by any means necessary.

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:08.450
And we know what some of those means are.

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:10.520
That's what I think would be the best.

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:14.940
Now, if you disagree with me or you agree
with me, whatever I want to hear from you,

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:16.050
let me know what you think.

